msgid "plugins.generic.disco.disco"
msgstr "Discoverability companion"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.description.long"
msgstr "Editors use the Plugin Discoverability companion to check various criteria and gain an overview of their journals. The requirements of aggregators, indexing databases, or search engines are divided into several sections. Some criteria are evaluated automatically, some editors must check themselves in a simple checklist, and others serve only as recommendations. Check to see if your journal could be more visible and learn how to achieve that."


msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.scholarlyJournal"
msgstr "Scholarly journal" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.scholarlyJournal.description"
msgstr "The journal should be a scholarly journal that selects papers via an explicitly described evaluation process before and/or after publication, in line with accepted practices in the relevant discipline (See also DOAS <a href="https://doi.org/10.58121/Z15S-JY03">https://doi.org/10.58121/Z15S-JY03</a>)" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond"
msgstr "Diamond criteria"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.description"
msgstr "The Diamond OA criteria for journals are a set of <strong>operational criteria</strong> that allow for a binary classification between Diamond OA journals (journals that fulfil all these criteria)and non-Diamond OA journals (journals that do not fulfil all these criteria)<br />Below are the 6 criteria as defined by the task force in collaboration with the community<br /><br />"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.openLicence"
msgstr "Open Access with open licenses" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.openLicence.description"
msgstr "All outputs of the journal should be Open Access and carry an open license that is included in the article-level metadata." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.noCharges"
msgstr "No fees" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.noCharges.description"
msgstr "Publication in the journal is not contingent on the payment of fees of any kind (e.g., article processing charges or membership dues). The journal should state this as such on its webpage. Voluntary author contributions and donations are allowed, if this is not a condition for publication.<p>Redalyc: The journal must not charge neither authors nor institutions for article assessment or processing.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.openAuthorship"
msgstr "Open to all authors" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.openAuthorship.description"
msgstr "<p>Authorship in the journal should not be limited to any type of affiliation. Any author can submit an article that is in line with the aims and scope of the journal.</p><p>After checking the checkbox and saving, a self-declaration text regarding openness to all authors will appear at the end of the \"About journal\" section.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.ownershipScience"
msgstr "Community-owned" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.ownershipScience.description"
msgstr "<p>The journal title must be owned by public or not-for-profit organisations (or parts there of) whose mission includes performing or promoting research and scholarship These include but are not limited to research performing organisations (RPOs), research funding organisations (RFOs), organisations connected to RPOs (university libraries, university presses, faculties, and departments), research institutes, and scholarly societies. The journal should explain its ownership status on its webpage.</p><p>After checking the checkbox and saving, a self-declaration text about ownership will appear at the end of the \"About journal\" section.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance"
msgstr "Appearance"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.description"
msgstr "This section focuses on the journal's online presence and accessibility. Ensuring that your journal meets key criteria like having a functional website, a clear and accurate journal title, and a quality English homepage can significantly enhance its visibility. Here, you'll evaluate whether your journal's full content is available online, confirm the availability of an eISSN, and check if the journal's content is open access. Use this overview to identify improvements that could make your journal more discoverable to readers and indexing services."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.functionalWebsite"
msgstr "Functional website" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.functionalWebsite.description"
msgstr "Website information must be accurate, and the information architecture and navigation system must ensure easy access to the published content and all other features defining the journal (such as Editorial Board, instructions to authors, peer review, access model, and so on). The journal website must clearly link to the publisher's website and vice versa." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.journalUrl"
msgstr "Journal URL" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.journalUrl.description"
msgstr "<p>Where both online and print editions are available, it is mandatory to provide the journal URL and full-text access details of current content.</p><p>The journal must have its dedicated URL and homepage that is accessible from any location.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.eIssn"
msgstr "Persistent identification (eISSN)" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.diamond.eIssn.description"
msgstr "<p>The journal must have a registered ISSN that is verifiable on the ISSN database (https://portal.issn.org/) and is clearly and consistently displayed on all journal platforms (electronic and/or print). If both print and electronic ISSNs are present, both should be provided.</p><p>ERIH PLUS requires a valid ISSN code, confirmed by the International ISSN Portal. Be advised that journals with ISSN codes listed as assigned to a publication but not yet confirmed or free ISSN will not be processed.</p>"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.fullContentAvailable"
msgstr "Full journal published content available (is the journal available?) - OA" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.fullContentAvailable.description"
msgstr "Is your journal Open Access and fully available online for free without any kind of registration" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.journalTitle"
msgstr "Journal Title" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.journalTitle.description"
msgstr "The journal must have a distinct title that is aligned with the registered ISSN, the journal's stated scope, published content, and community demographic (editorial board and authors). The title should be consistently displayed at the article, issue (if present), journal, and website levels." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.metaInformationFilled"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.metaInformationFilled.description"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.qualityEnHomepage"
msgstr "Quality homepage in English" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.appearance.qualityEnHomepage.description"
msgstr "Quality English language journal home page available" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription"
msgstr "Journal Description"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.description"
msgstr "This section focuses on ensuring that your journal provides essential information to establish its credibility, transparency, and accessibility. A well-documented description of aims and scope, clear author guidelines, editorial board details, and contact information are key to fostering trust with readers and contributors. Additionally, demonstrating adherence to ethical standards, transparency in the peer review process, and showcasing original scholarly articles contribute to the journal's visibility and reputation in the academic community."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.aimsAndScopeDescribed"
msgstr "Page with aims and scope" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.aimsAndScopeDescribed.description"
msgstr "The journal must have a well-defined scope and statement of purpose showing focus and coherence. Published content must be consistent with the title and stated scope of the journal, and where relevant, the special issue in which it is published. <br /> Who is the journal intended for?" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.authorGuidelinesDescribed"
msgstr "Guidelines for Authors are well described" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.authorGuidelinesDescribed.description"
msgstr "Instructions for authors are properly described, preferably in English language." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.bibliographicInformation"
msgstr "Bibliographic Information in Roman Script" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.bibliographicInformation.description"
msgstr "Cited references, names, and affiliations must be published in Roman script to allow rapid, accurate indexing and easy comprehension by global users." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.editorialBoardPage"
msgstr "Editorial board with affiliation details" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.editorialBoardPage.description"
msgstr "Editorial Board Members must be identifiable and available for contact. Names and institutional affiliations - including country/region - of all members of the editorial team are required (such as Editor-in-Chief, Editorial Board Members, Associate Editors, Regional Editors, etc.). These details must also be provided for Guest Editors of special issues. Persistent digital identifiers (such as ResearcherID or ORCID) or links to institutional profiles may be provided to specify the identity and affiliation of Editorial Board Members.
ERIH PLUS requires that the members of the academic editorial board are listed, along with their affiliations (universities or other independent research institutions)." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.contactDetailsAvailable"
msgstr "Contact details available" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.contactDetailsAvailable.description"
msgstr "OJS checks if the contact details are filled in. <br /> Contact details for the journal's primary editorial and production roles must be provided. Email should be publicly available." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.editorialBoardPageExists"
msgstr "Is the editorial board field filled in OJS?" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.editorialBoardPageExists.description"
msgstr "OJS checks if the editorial board page exists in OJS." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.journalPublisherNameAvailable"
msgstr "The Journal's publisher name is available on the webpage" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.journalPublisherNameAvailable.description"
msgstr "OJS check if the journal's publisher name is filled in. <br />The publisher name must be clearly defined, and a verifiable, physical address (not P.O. Box) for the publisher's business offices must be provided. If there is a society affiliation or ownership, this should be stated, and verifiable contact information must be provided." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.peerReviewDescribed"
msgstr "Peer review process described" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.peerReviewDescribed.description"
msgstr "The journal must provide a readily accessible, clear statement of its commitment to peer review and/or editorial oversight of all published content. Primary research articles must be subject to external peer review. <br />
Published content must reflect adequate and effective peer review and/or editorial oversight. Signs of deficient peer review include, but are not limited to, articles that demonstrate lack of scholarly rigor or scientific validity, presence of articles outside the scope of the journal or irrelevant citations.<br />
ERIH PLUS requires an explicit description of the journal's procedures for external/independent peer review. As a minimum, the journal's website must describe how the process ensures that reviewers are independent of the 
" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.publicationEthicsDescribed"
msgstr "Publication ethics are well described" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.publicationEthicsDescribed.description"
msgstr "The publication ethics and publication malpractice statement have to be publicly available. <br /> The journal must be transparent about its ethical requirements for authors and published works. If the journal supports and uses one or more third-party organizations' principles (WAME, COPE, Declaration of Helsinki, etc.), either the full text of the guidelines should be presented and appropriately credited to the source, or a functioning link to the full text of the guideline should be provided." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.scholarlyArticles"
msgstr "Original scholarly articles" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalDescription.scholarlyArticles.description"
msgstr "The journal must contain primarily original scholarly material. The academic level of the research reported should be appropriate to a graduate, post-doctoral, and/or professional research audience.<br />Redalyc: From each instalment, at least 75% of all contributions must be original research outcomes as well as other significant contributions and novel to the journal's particular field. (BCA)." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys"
msgstr "Landing Pages / Galleys"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.description"
msgstr "This category ensures that each article and its associated content are presented in a structured and accessible manner. Key elements include full bibliographic information, clear access to full-text content, DOI displayed as a URL, proper citations, and unique URLs for articles and their galleys to enhance discoverability and citation accuracy."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.dataInJats"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.dataInJats.description"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.lpDoi"
msgstr "The DOI is displayed as a URL" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.lpDoi.description"
msgstr "So that if a reader wishes to cite this item, they can just copy and paste the DOI link (learn more about Crossref <a href="https://www.crossref.org/display-guidelines" target="_blank">DOI display guidelines</a>)" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.linkToFulltext"
msgstr "A way to access the full-text of the content" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.linkToFulltext.description"
msgstr "It's acceptable for the full-text to be behind a login or paywall - this is fine as long as the landing page is accessible to everyone. A DOI can resolve to the HTML full-text of the content, and if this page includes the criteria above, a separate landing page is not necessary. It's not good practice to link directly to a PDF, however, as it will start downloading when the DOI is clicked." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.references"
msgstr "Appropriate Citations to the Literature (References on the Landing Pages)" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.references.description"
msgstr "It is expected that articles will appropriately acknowledge the surrounding literature for the topic." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.fullBio"
msgstr "Full bibliographic information" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.fullBio.description"
msgstr "So that the user can verify they have been delivered to the correct item by DOI." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.uniqueUrlArticles"
msgstr "Unique URL per Article (Landing Pages) and each Galleys" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.lpGalleys.uniqueUrlArticles.description"
msgstr "Each article must be available as an individual, full-text article. One unique URL per article: (HTML or PDF, as a minimum).<br/> It will be effectively indexed when each article has its URL." 


msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements"
msgstr "Metadata Requirements"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.description"
msgstr "This category focuses on the quality and completeness of metadata to improve the journal's discoverability and interoperability. Key aspects include specifying author affiliations, providing metadata in machine-readable formats with meta tags, utilizing the OAI-PMH protocol, assigning DOIs, including titles and abstracts in English, and properly marking references for accurate indexing and citation."


msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.metadataFormatOpenAIRE"
msgstr "OpenAIRE metadataPrefix" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.metadataFormatOpenAIRE.description"
msgstr "OpenAIRE expects metadata to be encoded following the metadata format defined in the OpenAIRE Application Profile. The recommended metadataPrefix is oai_openaire. For information on how to use the individual properties, please refer to the section <a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/application_profile.html#application-profile" target="_blank">Application Profile Overview.</a><p>In OJS you can use <a href="https://github.com/munipress/openAIREstandard" target="_blank">openAIREstandard plugin</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.markingReferences"
msgstr "Marking the references" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.markingReferences.description"
msgstr "Mark the section of the paper that contains references to other works with a standard heading, such as "References" or "Bibliography", on a line by itself. Individual references inside this section should be either numbered "1. - 2. - 3." or "[1] - [2] - [3]" in PDF, or put inside an "&lt;ol&gt;" list in HTML. The text of each reference must be a formal bibliographic citation in a commonly used format, without free-form commentary." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.authorsAffiliations"
msgstr "Author affiliation details specified" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.authorsAffiliations.description"
msgstr "Authors of all scholarly works must be accurately identified. Names and institutional affiliations - including country/region - of all contributing authors are required. Persistent digital identifiers (such as ResearcherID or ORCID) or links to institutional profiles may be provided to specify the identity and affiliation of authors.</p><p>ERIH PLUS requires information on author affiliations for all scholarly articles for the last two years of publication, i.e., the full names of the respective universities or other independent research institutions. ERIH PLUS also encourages journals to include author addresses (either email or postal addresses).</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.machineReadableMetadataFormat"
msgstr "Metadata in machine-readable format - meta tags" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.machineReadableMetadataFormat.description"
msgstr "If you're using repository or journal management software, such as Eprints, DSpace, Digital Commons, or OJS, please configure it to export bibliographic data in HTML "&lt;meta&gt;" tags. Google Scholar supports Highwire Press tags (e.g., citation_title), Eprints tags (e.g., eprints.title), BE Press tags (e.g., bepress_citation_title), and PRISM tags (e.g., prism.title). Use Dublin Core tags (e.g., DC.title) as a last resort - they work poorly for journal papers because Dublin Core doesn't have unambiguous fields for journal title, volume, issue, and page numbers. To check that these tags are present, visit several abstracts and view their HTML source." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.metadataInDCFormat"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.metadataInDCFormat.description"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.oaiPMHEnabled"
msgstr "Using the OAI-PMH protocol" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.oaiPMHEnabled.description"
msgstr "The providers can have their contents indexed on GoTriple in three ways: - by following the GoTriple recommendations for the technical set-up and the data model, i.e., using the OAI-PMH protocol and  the DC metadata standard. </p><p>For OpenAIRE, this is the only possible way to register and index the metadata there. For the "OpenAIRE Guidelines for Literature, institutional, and thematic Repositories v 4.0", you have to use the <em>metadataPrefix</em> <strong>oai_openaire</strong>. You can use the OJS plugin: <a href='https://github.com/munipress/openAIREstandard' target='_blank'>https://github.com/munipress/openAIREstandard</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.systemLanguageCheck"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.systemLanguageCheck.description"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.usingDOIs"
msgstr "Using DOIs" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.usingDOIs.description"
msgstr "Does the journal have a Digital Identifier (like DOI) or is it a member of Crossref?" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.titlesAbstractsInEnglish"
msgstr "Titles and abstracts in English" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataRequirements.titlesAbstractsInEnglish.description"
msgstr "Regardless of the language of the main body of published content, the journal must provide an accurate, comprehensible English language translation of all article titles. Scholarly articles must have abstracts, and those abstracts must be translated into English.<p>Clarity of abstracts.</p><p>ERIH PLUS requires that all original articles be accompanied by abstracts in English. As the ERIH PLUS team needs access to the abstracts to evaluate the journal, they should be available online.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality"
msgstr "Metadata Quality"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.description"
msgstr "An overview of the metadata requirements for various databases and services. Users can find a list of key metadata fields and their importance in enhancing visibility and increasing the chances of successful indexing. The page serves as a reference guide, helping users understand which metadata is essential for specific databases and supporting their proper utilization."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.accessRights"
msgstr "Access Rights" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.accessRights.description"
msgstr "Information about the rights or mode in which resource can be accessed. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_accessrights.html#dci-accessrights" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_accessrights.html#dci-accessrights</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.alternateIdentifier"
msgstr "Alternate Identifier" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.alternateIdentifier.description"
msgstr "Typically persistent identifier (for example: DOI, Handle, PURL, â€¦)<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_alternativeidentifier.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_alternativeidentifier.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.articleEndPage"
msgstr "Article End Page / Citation End Page" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.articleEndPage.description"
msgstr "OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationendpage.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationendpage.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.articleStartPage"
msgstr "Article Start Page / Citation Start Page" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.articleStartPage.description"
msgstr "OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationstartpage.html">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationstartpage.html</a></p> 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.audience"
msgstr "Audience" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.audience.description"
msgstr "A class of entity for whom the resource is intended or useful.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_audience.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_audience.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.authors"
msgstr "Creators / Authors" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.authors.description"
msgstr "The authors of the publication are listed in priority order. May be a corporate/institutional or personal name.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_creator.html#dci-creator" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_creator.html#dci-creator</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.contributors"
msgstr "Contributor" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.contributors.description"
msgstr "The institution or person responsible for collecting, managing, distributing, or otherwise contributing to the development of the resource.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_contributor.html#dci-contributor" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_contributor.html#dci-contributor</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.coverage"
msgstr "Coverage" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.coverage.description"
msgstr "The extent or scope of the content of the resource. Coverage will typically include a temporal period (a period label, date, or date range) or jurisdiction (such as a named administrative entity). <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_coverage.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_coverage.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.embargoPeriodDate"
msgstr "Embargo Period Date" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.embargoPeriodDate.description"
msgstr "Dates relevant to describe an embargo period.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_embargoenddate.html#dci-dateembargo" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_embargoenddate.html#dci-dateembargo</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.fileLocation"
msgstr "File Location" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.fileLocation.description"
msgstr "An unambiguous reference to the files, e.g., fulltext, the resource is associated with.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_filelocation.html#aire-file" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_filelocation.html#aire-file</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.format"
msgstr "Format" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.format.description"
msgstr "Format of the content based on MIME types. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_format.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_format.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.fundingReferences"
msgstr "Funding Reference" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.fundingReferences.description"
msgstr "Information about financial support (funding) for the resource being registered.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_projectid.html#aire-fundingreference" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_projectid.html#aire-fundingreference</a></p> <p>In OJS you should use <a href="https://github.com/ajnyga/funding" target="_blank">Funding Plugin</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.geoLocation"
msgstr "Geo Location" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.geoLocation.description"
msgstr "Spatial region or named place where the data was gathered or about which the data is focused.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_geolocation.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_geolocation.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.issueNumber"
msgstr "Issue number / Citation Issue" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.issueNumber.description"
msgstr "OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationissue.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationissue.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.issueVolume"
msgstr "Issue Volume / Citation Volume" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.issueVolume.description"
msgstr "This property is considered to be part of the bibliographic citation. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationvolume.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationvolume.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.journalTitle"
msgstr "Journal Title / Citation Title" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.journalTitle.description"
msgstr "OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationtitle.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_citationtitle.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.language"
msgstr "Language" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.language.description"
msgstr "A language of the intellectual content of the resource.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_language.html#dc-language" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_language.html#dc-language</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.licenseCondition"
msgstr "License Condition" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.licenseCondition.description"
msgstr "Information about license rights held in and over the resource.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_licensecondition.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_licensecondition.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.publicationDate"
msgstr "Publication Date" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.publicationDate.description"
msgstr "A date associated with an event in the life cycle of the resource. Typically, Date will be associated with the creation or availability of the resource. Recommended best practice for encoding the date value is defined in a profile of ISO 8601 [W3CDTF] and follows the YYYY-MM-DD format.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_publicationdate.html#dci-datepublication" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_publicationdate.html#dci-datepublication</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.publisher"
msgstr "Publisher" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.publisher.description"
msgstr "An entity responsible for making the resource available. Examples of a Publisher include a person, an organization, or a service. Typically, the name of a Publisher should be used to indicate the entity.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_publisher.html#dc-publisher" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_publisher.html#dc-publisher</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.relatedIdentifier"
msgstr "Related Identifier" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.relatedIdentifier.description"
msgstr "An identifier of a related resource other than the primary Identifier applied to the resource being registered.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_relatedidentifier.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_relatedidentifier.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceIdentifier"
msgstr "Resource Identifier" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceIdentifier.description"
msgstr "Practically a stable, persistent URL. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_resourceidentifier.html#dci-identifier" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_resourceidentifier.html#dci-identifier</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceType"
msgstr "Resource Type" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceType.description"
msgstr "The type of scientific output the resource is a manifestation of. It describes the genre of the resource.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_publicationtype.html#aire-resourcetype" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_publicationtype.html#aire-resourcetype</a></p><p>In OJS you should use <a href="https://github.com/munipress/openAIREstandard" target="_blank">openAIREstandard plugin</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceVersion"
msgstr "Resource Version" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceVersion.description"
msgstr "The status in the publication process of journal articles.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_resourceversion.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_resourceversion.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.size"
msgstr "Size" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.size.description"
msgstr "Number of pages or filesize.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_size.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_size.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.source"
msgstr "Source" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.source.description"
msgstr "A reference to a resource from which the present resource is derived.<p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Recommended / Optional</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_source.html" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_source.html</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.subject"
msgstr "Subject" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.subject.description"
msgstr "Subject, keyword, classification code, or key phrase describing the resource. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required if applicable</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_subject.html#dci-subject" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_subject.html#dci-subject</a> </p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.title"
msgstr "Title" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.title.description"
msgstr "A name or title by which a resource is known. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_title.html#dci-title" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_title.html#dci-title</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.abstract"
msgstr "Description" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.abstract.description"
msgstr "This element is used for a textual description of the content. <p>OpenAIRE: <strong>Required</strong></p><p><a href="https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_description.html#dc-description" target="_blank">https://openaire-guidelines-for-literature-repository-managers.readthedocs.io/en/v4.0.0/field_description.html#dc-description</a></p>"


msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.title.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with titles in the journal's primary localization filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.authors.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with at least one affiliated author."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.publicationDate.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with a publication date filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.resourceType.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles in sections with filled in resource types."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.abstract.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with abstracts in the journal's primary localization filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.embargoPeriodDate.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles in issues with embargo period dates that are not immediately open access."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.language.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with primary localization filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.alternateIdentifier.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with DOIs connected."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.source.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with a source in the journal's primary localization filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.licenseCondition.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with alicense type filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.coverage.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with a coverage in the journal's primary localization filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.metadataQuality.size.countCheck"
msgstr "The number of articles with pages filled in."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy"
msgstr "Journal policy"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.description"
msgstr "This category ensures transparency and accessibility by outlining the journal's policies. It covers details such as APC practices, open access policies (including Creative Commons or equivalent), copyright terms, and the absence of embargo periods. Additionally, it confirms whether users can freely access content without registration, emphasizing inclusivity and openness."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.apcDescribed"
msgstr "APC policy description"  

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.apcDescribed.description"
msgstr "The fee policy should be described on the webpage. No matter if the journal has APCs or not.<p>DOAJ: If a journal doesn't have any charges, then this must be stated. <br/>ERIH Plus: Does the journal have an APC? If so, is it on the high or low end?</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.noRegistrationNeed"
msgstr "Users don't need to register" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.noRegistrationNeed.description"
msgstr "No requirement for users to register to read the content of the journal." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.oaPolicyDescribed"
msgstr "Open Access policy described (CC or equivalent)" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.oaPolicyDescribed.description"
msgstr "Journals where the copyright holder of a scholarly work grants usage rights to others using an open license (Creative Commons or equivalent). This allows for immediate free access to the work and permits any user to read, download, copy, distribute, print, search, or link to the full texts of articles, crawl them for indexing, pass them as data to software, or use them for any other lawful purpose.<p>REDALYC: The journal must allow reading, downloading, copying, distributing, printing, searching, or linking to its full text articles.</p><p>The licensing terms for use and re-use of the published content must be clearly stated on the website. <br/>DOAJ recommends using Creative Commons licenses for this purpose.<br />If Creative Commons licensing is not used, similar terms and conditions should be applied. (Extra care must be taken to state these terms clearly.)<br />It is recommended that licensing information is displayed or embedded in full-text articles, but this is not required for inclusion in DOAJ.</p><p>ERIH Plus: What is the Open Access status of the journal?</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.copyrightTerms"
msgstr "Copyright terms described" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.copyrightTerms.description"
msgstr "The copyright terms applied to the published content must be clearly stated and separate from those applied to the website.<br />Copyright terms must not contradict the licensing terms or the terms of the open access policy.<br />"All rights reserved" is never appropriate for open access content.<br /><a href="https://doaj.org/apply/copyright-and-licensing/" target="_blank">More about copyright</a>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.noEmbargoPeriod"
msgstr "No embargo period" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.journalPolicy.noEmbargoPeriod.description"
msgstr "The full text of all content must be available for free and open access without delay." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity"
msgstr "Regularity"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.description"
msgstr "This category evaluates the journal's consistency and reliability in publishing. It considers regular periodicity, a well-documented publishing history, and adherence to timely publication schedules or defined publication volumes, ensuring the journal maintains a dependable presence in the academic community."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.periodicity"
msgstr "Regular periodicity" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.periodicity.description"
msgstr "Journal has to publish on a regular basis. No delays or interruptions in the publication schedule.<p>REDALYC: Instalments must be published on time according to the publication schedule (monthly, bimonthly, quarterly). If periodical, a period exceeding three months without publishing new articles online will be disadvantageous.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.publishingHistory"
msgstr "Publishing history" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.publishingHistory.description"
msgstr "DOAJ: Journal must demonstrate a publishing history of more than one year or have published at least ten open access research articles.<p>ERIH Plus: Does the journal have a publication history of at least two years?</p><p>PubMed: NLM expects publishers to have at least a two-year history of quality scholarly publishing in the life sciences. / A minimum of 25 peer reviewed articles (e.g., original research or review articles, clinical case reports) must be published in final form.</p><p>Redalyc: The journal must have been active for at least two years. Instalments edited during the last two years must be visible on their platform. For assessment purposes, only regular issues edited on time will be considered.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.timeliness"
msgstr "Timeliness and/or Publication Volume" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.regularity.timeliness.description"
msgstr "The journal must state whether it has a defined publication frequency or if it operates under an irregular or continuous publication schedule. The journal must conform to the stated schedule. The volume of scholarly articles published annually should demonstrate that the journal is attracting sufficient interest from the relevant scholarly community to be sustainable. The journal must also have published enough content across the breadth of its scope to allow comprehensive evaluation." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations"
msgstr "General Recommendations"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.description"
msgstr "This category emphasizes best practices for maintaining a high-quality journal. It includes clarity of language, adherence to community standards, validity of published statements, transparency about grant support, the use of reliable internal systems (e.g., OJS, Lodel), and the implementation of plagiarism checks to ensure academic integrity."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.accesibility"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.accesibility.description"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.clarityOfLanguage"
msgstr "Clarity of Language" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.clarityOfLanguage.description"
msgstr "For titles, abstracts, and all other published text presented in English, the language must be clear and comprehensible to a global audience." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.communityStandardsAdherence"
msgstr "Adherence to Community Standards" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.communityStandardsAdherence.description"
msgstr "Editorial policies are consistent with recognized best practices, such as COPE Core Practices, and/or national and international organizations and scholarly societies that advance principles for research integrity within their communities. Articles in the journal are consistent with accepted best practices in their subject area (for example, accepted standards in organism or chemical nomenclature)." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.grantSupportDetails"
msgstr "Grant Support Details" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.grantSupportDetails.description"
msgstr "In subject areas where grant support is common or required, appropriate acknowledgement regarding the source of funding is recommended." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.statementsValidity"
msgstr "Validity of Statements" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.statementsValidity.description"
msgstr "Published content should demonstrate adherence to the policies declared by the journal. All information displayed on the journal website should be accurate and up to date. It is not the intention of our review to enforce ethical and plagiarism standards. " 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.internalSystemInUse"
msgstr "Internal system in use (OJS / Lodel /...)" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.internalSystemInUse.description"
msgstr "Will ensure that many requirements are met automatically." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.plagiarismCheck"
msgstr "Plagiarism check implemented" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.generalRecommendations.plagiarismCheck.description"
msgstr "Use of a plagiarism checking service is highly recommended but not required for inclusion in DOAJ." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations"
msgstr "Impact Recommendations"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.description"
msgstr "This category focuses on enhancing the journal's academic influence and reputation. It focuses on the geographical diversity of authors and the editorial board, analyzes citation metrics for both authors and board members, assesses the citedness of journal articles, and emphasizes the significance of the content's academic contribution to its field."

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.authorsDiversity"
msgstr "Diversity in the geographical distribution of authors" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.authorsDiversity.description"
msgstr "The authors must have affiliations, geographic diversity, and publication records that validate their participation in the scholarly community associated with the stated scope of the journal.<p>DOAJ: The proportion of published research papers where at least one of the authors is an editor, editorial board member, or reviewer must not exceed 25% in either of the latest two issues</p><p>ERIH PLUS requires that no more than two thirds of the authors published in the journal are from the same institution. The authorship of journals is determined by reviewing the last two years of publication.</p><p>REDALYC: At least 70% of all scholarly works published on each issue must be contributions external to the publishing institution (with at least one external author).</p><p>Endogeny should be minimised.</p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.citedAuthors"
msgstr "Author Citation Analysis" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.citedAuthors.description"
msgstr "Most authors should have a discernible publication history in the Web of Science. Authors' citation networks should be appropriate to the category and journals of comparable scope." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.citedEditorialBoard"
msgstr "Editorial Board Citation Analysis" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.citedEditorialBoard.description"
msgstr "Most Editorial Board Members should have a discernible publication history in the Web of Science. Editorial Board Members' citation networks should be appropriate to the category and journals of comparable scope." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.citedness"
msgstr "Citedness of journal articles" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.citedness.description"
msgstr "Most selective indices contain the most impactful journals in their discipline. In the comparative citation analysis, both the number and the sources of the citations to the journal are taken into consideration. The stability of citation activity is also considered, as we are looking not only at the influence of a journal in a given year but also the sustainability of that influence." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.contentSignificance"
msgstr "Content Significance / Academic contribution to the field" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.contentSignificance.description"
msgstr "The content in the journal should be of interest, importance, and value to its intended readership and Web of Science subscribers. Content significance may be evidenced as a unique specialization, novel perspective, regional focus, unusual content, or content that enriches the breadth of Web of Science coverage. These attributes are not exclusively reflected in journal-level citation activity." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.editorsDiversity"
msgstr "Diversity in the geographical distribution of the editorial board" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.impactRecommendations.editorsDiversity.description"
msgstr "Editor and Editorial Board Member affiliations, geographic diversity, and publication records must be consistent with the stated scope and published content of the journal. The size and composition of the Editorial Board must be consistent with the volume and breadth of publication output. Due consideration will be given to journals that employ full-time professional editors." 


msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo"
msgstr "SEO"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.description"
msgstr "SEO (Search Engine Optimization) is the practice of optimizing a website or online content to improve its visibility on search engine results pages (SERPs). The goal is to attract organic (non-paid) traffic by ensuring the site ranks higher for relevant keywords and phrases. SEO involves various strategies, including optimizing on-page elements like content, meta tags, and headings; improving technical aspects like site speed, mobile-friendliness, and structured data; and building high-quality backlinks to boost authority. Effective SEO not only enhances search rankings but also improves user experience, driving more engaged visitors and increasing conversion potential.<p>What is SEO for beginners: <a href="https://www.elegantthemes.com/blog/marketing/what-is-seo" target="_blank">https://www.elegantthemes.com/blog/marketing/what-is-seo</a></p>"

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.accurateTitles"
msgstr "Accurate page titles " 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.accurateTitles.description"
msgstr "Choose terms for your page titles that match the content of your documents. Users are more likely to click a link if the title matches their search." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.altTextImages"
msgstr "ALT text for images" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.altTextImages.description"
msgstr "ALT text improves the searchability of the image content of your pages. It also makes your pages more accessible to text-only browsers and visually impaired site visitors." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.articlesInHtml"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.articlesInHtml.description"
msgstr "" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.covers"
msgstr "Issues' / Journal's cover" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.covers.description"
msgstr "Helps users with "by image" searching." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.crosslinks"
msgstr "Meaningful cross-links" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.crosslinks.description"
msgstr "Meaningful links between your website and other related websites and providers of relevant content add value for visitors and can boost your ranking." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.h1Title"
msgstr "Journal Title in H1" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.h1Title.description"
msgstr "Helps the search engines to correctly identify the page title." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.keyTerms"
msgstr "Key terms" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.keyTerms.description"
msgstr "When building your website's text and pages, it's a good idea to research and use key terms that your audience uses to search for your type of content." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.noTextInImages"
msgstr "Avoid text in images" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.noTextInImages.description"
msgstr "Keep relevant text and links in HTML. Encoding your text in graphics or image maps can prevent search engines from finding the text or following links to your website's other pages." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.pageLoadingTime"
msgstr "Improve page loading times" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.pageLoadingTime.description"
msgstr "Page speed affects your SEO a lot. Maybe more than anything other than having fantastic content that directly addresses your users' search queries. Over the past few years, Google has adjusted its algorithm to take user experience into account. One of the top factors for a good user experience is having a quick and responsive site." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.readableURLs"
msgstr "Readable URLs" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.readableURLs.description"
msgstr "Use URLs that represent the content pages, instead of numeric or otherwise cryptic URLs." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.robotsFile"
msgstr "Robots.txt file" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.robotsFile.description"
msgstr "Create robots.txt file for search engines.<p> <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/robots/intro" target="_blank">Introduction to robots.txt file.</a></p>" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.robotsMetadata"
msgstr "Robots Metadata" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.robotsMetadata.description"
msgstr "Use a "Description" meta-tag and write your description accurately and carefully. After the title, the description is the most important draw for users. Make sure the document title and description attract the interest of the user as well as match the content on your site." 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.seoCompliant"
msgstr "Check your page SEO compliance" 

msgid "plugins.generic.disco.seo.seoCompliant.description"
